  "description": "#3892 — the three value-shape arms of `filtered_blocks_query_inner`'s per-filter dispatch that had never been exercised, plus the key-presence arm that has no value predicate at all. Before #3892 the ratchet keyed on the COMMAND, and `filtered_blocks_status_open` (the `valueText` arm, in `query_reads_links_search_pages`) made the whole command read as covered while `valueTextIn` / `valueDate` / `valueDateRange` / no-value emitted SQL nothing had ever compared across the two stacks. Every step below is authored to fail for a SPECIFIC reason a plausible implementation gets wrong (set membership vs first-element, date column vs text column, half-open vs closed range, key-scoped EXISTS vs any-property EXISTS) rather than to pin one obvious row. Non-reserved keys throughout: a reserved key (`todo_state` / `priority` / `due_date` / `scheduled_date`) routes to a direct `b.<col>` predicate instead, which is a second dispatch dimension this fixture deliberately does not mix in.",
