      "command": "filtered_blocks_query",
      "comment": "#3892 `valueTextIn` arm — `value_text IN (SELECT value FROM json_each(?N))`. Discriminating because BOTH members must match: an implementation that compared against the first element only (or that bound the JSON array as a scalar) returns a strict subset. S5/S6 own a `due` but no `status`, so they must be excluded — the EXISTS is key-scoped, not block-scoped.",
      "name": "filtered_value_text_in_matches_either_member"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "limit": 100,
        "propertyFilters": [
          {
            "key": "due",
            "operator": "eq",
            "valueDate": "2026-08-10"
          }
        ],
        "scope": {
          "kind": "active",
          "space_id": "$SPACE"
        }
      },
      "command": "filtered_blocks_query",
      "comment": "#3892 `valueDate` arm — `value_date = ?N`. Discriminating because the value lives in the `value_date` column, not `value_text`: an implementation that compared the wrong typed column returns nothing at all. S5's `2026-08-15` and S6's `2026-08-16` are near misses on the same key.",
      "name": "filtered_value_date_exact"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "limit": 100,
        "propertyFilters": [
          {
            "key": "due",
            "operator": "eq",
            "valueDateRange": ["2026-08-10", "2026-08-16"]
          }
        ],
        "scope": {
          "kind": "active",
          "space_id": "$SPACE"
        }
      },
      "command": "filtered_blocks_query",
      "comment": "#3892 `valueDateRange` arm — `value_date >= ?from AND value_date < ?to`, a HALF-OPEN interval. Both bounds are pinned by a row: S2 sits exactly on `from` (an exclusive lower bound drops it) and S6 sits exactly on `to` (an inclusive upper bound admits it). S3's `2026-09-20` is far outside.",
      "name": "filtered_value_date_range_is_half_open"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "limit": 100,
        "propertyFilters": [
